WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:03.744
In Kyiv central train station

00:00:03.744 --> 00:00:05.870
and about to go to Kharkiv

00:00:06.288 --> 00:00:11.672
and Kharkiv, I've done about
five minute of research on this place.

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:15.909
So I have absolutely no idea
what I'm getting into.

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.115
[train station announcement]

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:38.605
♪ deep house music ♪

00:00:57.703 --> 00:00:59.223
Kharkiv, Ukraine...

00:00:59.528 --> 00:01:02.128
Way out in the far East of the country.

00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:04.293
30 kilometers from the Russian border.

00:01:04.293 --> 00:01:08.585
First impressions, it was dark
but I could see a lot of street life.

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:10.275
Like a lot of people on the street

00:01:10.275 --> 00:01:11.875
lot of young people.

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:13.756
♪ busker playing guitar ♪

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.430
[music fades]

00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:24.472
[exhales]

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:25.968
Day one.

00:01:26.241 --> 00:01:28.425
These building here, this architecture

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:30.949
it does it for me, this constructivism.

00:01:30.949 --> 00:01:32.649
Such creative lines.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:35.729
Such beautiful proportions

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.521
They have a building here,
I think it's the opera house.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:44.110
Like a small planet landed on earth.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:48.530
It's just this massive hunk of weight.

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:52.024
It's so ugly, it's a little bit beautiful.

00:01:52.498 --> 00:01:54.965
There's all these kids outside of it.

00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:56.945
Skateboarding, people hanging out.

00:01:56.945 --> 00:01:58.563
There's fountains, it's nice.

00:01:58.563 --> 00:01:59.683
♪ deep house ♪

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.140
[skateboard clacking]

00:02:14.135 --> 00:02:17.035
Shashka is crushing it
on the skateboard here.

00:02:17.035 --> 00:02:18.220
Nice moves, Shashka.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.285
-How old are you?
-15.

00:02:20.446 --> 00:02:22.126
PETER: 15, nice, bro.

00:02:24.008 --> 00:02:25.048
[music fades]

00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:28.856
This is what I so much love about Ukraine.

00:02:28.856 --> 00:02:31.934
Is that it's properly mixed up.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.860
So you have that Soviet relic behind me

00:02:35.352 --> 00:02:36.352
and then...

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:38.574
[exhales]

00:02:38.728 --> 00:02:39.728
This.

00:02:41.263 --> 00:02:43.446
♪ melodic electronic ♪

00:03:48.072 --> 00:03:49.938
And then these side streets.

00:03:51.095 --> 00:03:52.775
Tree-lined side streets.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.028
Some quiet, some with little gardens.

00:03:55.028 --> 00:03:57.228
Like apartments, gardens, street.

00:03:57.455 --> 00:03:58.815
[music continues]

00:04:12.014 --> 00:04:13.054
[music fades]

00:04:14.703 --> 00:04:15.948
[radio advertisement]

00:04:22.806 --> 00:04:25.478
Okay, first impression of this square was

00:04:25.478 --> 00:04:28.990
"Okay, here's a
big cobblestone parking lot

00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:32.164
but then it opens up into this stuff.

00:04:32.164 --> 00:04:35.795
This is super impressive,
this architecture.

00:04:36.345 --> 00:04:37.967
And then you get into it

00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:39.007
and it's like

00:04:39.825 --> 00:04:40.825
design

00:04:42.278 --> 00:04:44.246
and style is in the DNA of this place

00:04:44.246 --> 00:04:46.246
because you go into that metro

00:04:46.493 --> 00:04:47.493
and

00:04:48.255 --> 00:04:50.000
it's the most beautiful metro I've seen.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.776
Like no joke, the most
outrageous metro stops.

00:04:57.131 --> 00:04:59.630
There was one that just
looked like a crazy science experiment.

00:04:59.936 --> 00:05:01.056
♪ electronic ♪

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.034
[metro slowing]

00:05:16.892 --> 00:05:18.412
♪ deep electronic ♪

00:05:39.049 --> 00:05:41.229
[doors close and safety horn sounds]

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.142
[train accelerates]

00:06:00.632 --> 00:06:01.672
[music fades]

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:04.391
A lot of eclectic businesses here.

00:06:04.391 --> 00:06:06.804
Like coffee shops, restaurants...

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:08.186
World class.

00:06:08.186 --> 00:06:10.466
You won't get these
in a lot of American cities.

00:06:10.466 --> 00:06:14.725
Like it's just not even
that progressive in many US cities.

00:06:14.725 --> 00:06:16.405
Even in a lot of Europe

00:06:16.405 --> 00:06:18.338
and then you find yourself...

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.550
You know...

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:22.128
Near the front lines of a war.

00:06:22.984 --> 00:06:25.397
A country that's
gone through a lot of turbulence.

00:06:25.397 --> 00:06:26.437
A lot, right?

00:06:26.851 --> 00:06:28.543
But there's this creative energy.

00:06:28.543 --> 00:06:31.699
Like there's this amazing
creative energy coming out of there

00:06:31.699 --> 00:06:34.799
and so it's designing,
building and operating

00:06:34.799 --> 00:06:36.453
all these cool businesses here.

00:06:36.453 --> 00:06:37.582
Very good.

00:06:37.582 --> 00:06:38.955
[Ukrainian]

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.032
PETER: And then there's, boom.

00:06:41.032 --> 00:06:42.851
This new cat parlor

00:06:43.273 --> 00:06:44.374
and it's beautiful.

00:06:44.374 --> 00:06:46.054
It's like, done well.

00:06:46.759 --> 00:06:48.009
And then you come out of that

00:06:48.009 --> 00:06:50.543
and there's a massive old Soviet mural

00:06:50.807 --> 00:06:55.351
and then there's one of the most
beautiful metro stations on the planet.

00:06:55.966 --> 00:06:57.830
And there's a tractor going by

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.963
and then there's a BMW going by.

00:07:00.426 --> 00:07:02.276
And then there's an amazing restaurant

00:07:02.276 --> 00:07:04.607
and then there's a place called Mafia.

00:07:04.607 --> 00:07:05.774
I don't know how the food...

00:07:05.774 --> 00:07:08.150
It's a chain, I doubt it's amazing food

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.892
but what I'm saying is it's like all...

00:07:10.892 --> 00:07:13.148
[woosh woosh woosh]

00:07:13.148 --> 00:07:16.196
It's either that extreme

00:07:17.307 --> 00:07:18.805
or the other extreme.

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:30.117
They seem to be enjoying themselves.

00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:33.117
Okay, there's a lot of
pessimistic negative bullsh*t.

00:07:33.117 --> 00:07:39.494
Got it, but there's also a lot of this
young, vibrant, positive energy here

00:07:39.972 --> 00:07:41.565
and it seems connected.

00:07:41.565 --> 00:07:44.562
It seems like
you're walking down the streets

00:07:44.562 --> 00:07:47.422
and you're part of something
bigger than yourself.

00:07:47.825 --> 00:07:50.333
Way more diverse
than anywhere I've seen in Ukraine so far.

00:07:50.333 --> 00:07:53.600
So you're seeing black people.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.286
You’re seeing Arabs.

00:07:55.286 --> 00:07:56.966
You're seeing Asians.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.939
It felt a little bit more
like home in that respect

00:08:00.939 --> 00:08:03.440
because it was all mixed up
and that's because of the universities.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.687
People come from all over
to go to these universities.

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:14.619
And then you got these parks, right?

00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:16.059
And these parks...

00:08:16.874 --> 00:08:19.605
Gorky Park was the one
I spent the most time in.

00:08:19.828 --> 00:08:21.348
Old ladies dancing.

00:08:21.572 --> 00:08:26.339
There's kids on carnival rides.

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:28.206
There's people riding bikes.

00:08:28.391 --> 00:08:30.599
There's quiet spaces.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.227
There's people shooting guns at balloons.

00:08:35.018 --> 00:08:36.527
It's all mixed...

00:08:36.527 --> 00:08:38.461
Oh, and all these ropes.

00:08:38.895 --> 00:08:41.095
These rope apparatuses for kids.

00:08:41.491 --> 00:08:43.824
It's like a kid's paradise in there.

00:08:45.351 --> 00:08:46.391
♪ indy rock ♪

00:09:01.642 --> 00:09:04.042
[people screaming on roller coaster]

00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:14.308
And it's buff, the grass, perfect.

00:09:14.767 --> 00:09:18.716
The whole space is like perfectly clean.

00:09:18.716 --> 00:09:21.097
There's all these cleaners out there
and the really take...

00:09:22.269 --> 00:09:25.069
They really take pride
in their parks here.

00:09:25.151 --> 00:09:26.993
There's no trash on the ground.

00:09:26.993 --> 00:09:27.993
It's nice.

00:09:28.231 --> 00:09:31.189
And so I walked around for a bit
and then took this gondola ride

00:09:31.189 --> 00:09:33.277
and there's a gondola in the park

00:09:33.277 --> 00:09:34.277
and

00:09:35.636 --> 00:09:38.174
cool unique experience for me.

00:09:38.593 --> 00:09:42.103
But if I'm gonna talk about a park
where people are connecting

00:09:42.103 --> 00:09:43.463
to take your kids

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.910
to do a whole host of different things

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:52.517
then Gorky Park is the coolest
number one place I've seen for that.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.391
Look, the Ukrainians know how
to do the whole park thing really well.

00:10:01.391 --> 00:10:03.100
Like professional.

00:10:03.858 --> 00:10:07.038
Where Americans are
crazy on the whole safety thing

00:10:07.038 --> 00:10:09.305
like safety warnings for everything.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:13.273
Ukraine goes
the opposite direction I'd say.

00:10:13.659 --> 00:10:14.700
For example.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:15.820
[latch clanks]

00:10:16.639 --> 00:10:19.523
[door creaks and latch closes]

00:10:19.832 --> 00:10:22.078
Doesn't really close either but...

00:10:22.078 --> 00:10:24.945
You could push it
and go flying out of this thing

00:10:24.945 --> 00:10:25.945
and

00:10:26.102 --> 00:10:27.701
I like the fact... [clears throat]

00:10:27.701 --> 00:10:30.709
Okay, you don't wanna
lose your kid flying out of a gondola

00:10:30.709 --> 00:10:32.365
but I think people get it.

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:34.165
They're not stupid about it

00:10:34.409 --> 00:10:37.358
but I like the fact
that you're responsible for yourself.

00:10:37.358 --> 00:10:40.490
There are no "No" signs.

00:10:42.546 --> 00:10:44.880
Little kid like hooking himself in.

00:10:45.501 --> 00:10:47.021
The kid's doing it

00:10:47.775 --> 00:10:50.188
and then he's gonna
fly across the zip line.

00:10:51.581 --> 00:10:54.072
There's no way that would exist at home

00:10:54.072 --> 00:10:56.894
because there'd be more safety precaution.

00:10:56.894 --> 00:10:58.974
There'd be like three people checking it.

00:10:58.974 --> 00:11:00.460
I don't know what's better or worse.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:03.724
Seriously I don't
but I sort of find it entertaining

00:11:04.188 --> 00:11:08.188
to observe this place and how free it is.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.218
Then I met this guy.

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:14.630
Okay, poor Daniel,
I captured him on the streets.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.570
Recently out of university.

00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:19.018
-Looks like what?
-Like Hogwarts.

00:11:19.301 --> 00:11:22.413
-From Harry Potter.
-Dude, I never read Harry Potter.

00:11:22.413 --> 00:11:25.357
-C'mon but you (saw) the movie?
-No, I haven't.

00:11:25.954 --> 00:11:28.541
-You have to, it's so beautiful.
-All right.

00:11:28.541 --> 00:11:29.761
Next time. [laughs]

00:11:29.761 --> 00:11:31.441
Like I think he's only...

00:11:32.111 --> 00:11:34.921
Sorry Daniel, I think
you're only 22, right?

00:11:34.921 --> 00:11:37.377
Or 23, but somewhere around there.

00:11:38.028 --> 00:11:41.192
That building
is like architecture porn though.

00:11:41.192 --> 00:11:41.913
[chuckles]

00:11:41.913 --> 00:11:43.116
You know what I mean?

00:11:43.116 --> 00:11:44.343
It's absolutely beautiful.

00:11:44.343 --> 00:11:44.976
DANIEL: Yes.

00:11:44.976 --> 00:11:46.671
PETER: But inside you're saying
it's a cockroach?

00:11:46.671 --> 00:11:48.719
There's nothing going on in there?

00:11:48.719 --> 00:11:52.665
When I moved to United States
and first see your cockroach

00:11:52.665 --> 00:11:54.430
I was so pissed off.

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.921
Wait, you saw your
first cockroach in the US?

00:11:56.921 --> 00:11:58.601
-Yes.
-Congratulations.

00:11:59.028 --> 00:12:01.894
Got a job for a trucking company,
actually an American company.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:05.723
So your roommate Simon has got to
live with you and your girlfriend?

00:12:05.723 --> 00:12:06.723
DANIEL: Yes.

00:12:07.365 --> 00:12:10.047
-Poor guy.
-No, I mean he like it.

00:12:10.576 --> 00:12:12.534
He likes it?
[laughing]

00:12:12.877 --> 00:12:14.950
That seems interesting,
let's talk a minute.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.946
No, no, you're taking it out of context.

00:12:16.946 --> 00:12:18.390
-No, I mean...
-I always do.

00:12:18.769 --> 00:12:21.790
You said we have to have a pass inside
to get into the university?

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.748
Yes, but we don't have it, so...

00:12:23.748 --> 00:12:26.763
But I'm in with
the Babushka Mafiosa in Kyiv

00:12:27.231 --> 00:12:29.800
and they're all connected
like Facebook and aspen trees.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.080
Do you think so?

00:12:31.271 --> 00:12:34.034
PETER: Babushka Mafiosa
knows more about you

00:12:34.034 --> 00:12:35.928
-than you know about yourself.
-Yeah.

00:12:35.928 --> 00:12:38.528
She knows if you're gonna be successful.

00:12:39.124 --> 00:12:40.868
If it's gonna work out
with your girlfriend.

00:12:40.868 --> 00:12:42.182
Will you get married?

00:12:42.182 --> 00:12:44.072
All these things
you don't even know right now.

00:12:45.935 --> 00:12:48.257
Check it out, you know why this is here?

00:12:48.257 --> 00:12:48.828
DAVID: No.

00:12:48.828 --> 00:12:53.351
PETER: In the metro
it's this door that comes over.

00:12:53.351 --> 00:12:54.351
DAVID: Okay.

00:12:54.675 --> 00:12:56.875
And this, what you're standing on

00:12:57.623 --> 00:13:01.605
Stalin built them this way
as a bomb shelter.

00:13:02.086 --> 00:13:04.654
-So seriously if the nukes came...
-Seriously?

00:13:04.902 --> 00:13:08.102
The population of the city
would come down in here.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.979
Maybe in the United States of Ukraine.

00:13:10.979 --> 00:13:12.019
No, no, no...

00:13:12.019 --> 00:13:13.699
Designer doesn't care.

00:13:13.921 --> 00:13:16.788
No, no, this is
why it was built, seriously.

00:13:16.873 --> 00:13:19.881
-That's what I was told at least.
-Who told you?

00:13:20.739 --> 00:13:23.406
Uh, I don't remember,
it was a while ago.

00:13:24.333 --> 00:13:26.013
How do I say it? Like...

00:13:26.849 --> 00:13:29.624
There's a lot of
mature young people I would say.

00:13:29.888 --> 00:13:32.548
I have been in Spain over there

00:13:32.966 --> 00:13:36.345
and Poland but it doesn't count
because Poland is almost Ukraine.

00:13:36.345 --> 00:13:39.603
-Okay.
-And I will move to Georgia in November.

00:13:39.603 --> 00:13:43.311
So during one year
it's gonna be my third country.

00:13:43.311 --> 00:13:45.351
-So I mean...
-Dude, that's amazing.

00:13:45.351 --> 00:13:46.351
It's enough.

00:13:47.187 --> 00:13:48.613
Still not enough for my girlfriend.

00:13:48.613 --> 00:13:50.293
♪ Hare Krishna buskers  ♪

00:13:59.098 --> 00:14:00.096
Oh, yeah.

00:14:00.096 --> 00:14:01.296
Very good book.

00:14:03.416 --> 00:14:07.842
Recommendation for my friends in USA,
very good book.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.040
Look at that, man.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.040
That's cool.

00:14:12.316 --> 00:14:13.516
[Peter exhales]

00:14:14.866 --> 00:14:15.906
That is huge.

00:14:17.034 --> 00:14:18.483
That's what she said.

00:14:18.483 --> 00:14:19.483
[David giggles]

00:14:19.483 --> 00:14:21.305
-Do you know that joke?
-Yes, I know.

00:14:21.305 --> 00:14:23.071
It's from Wayne's World.

00:14:23.071 --> 00:14:25.737
A movie in the 80s before you were born.

00:14:26.474 --> 00:14:28.664
Okay, you're so old so you remember.

00:14:28.664 --> 00:14:30.233
So old I could be your dad.

00:14:30.233 --> 00:14:32.281
-We already went over this.
-Yeah.

00:14:32.281 --> 00:14:34.559
You didn't believe me but it's true.

00:14:34.559 --> 00:14:37.667
PETER: And there's an amazing amount
of wisdom I would say.

00:14:37.667 --> 00:14:40.283
Maybe I was just totally lucky
but I don't think that's the case.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.892
I actually do think
that's in sort of like the...

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:46.888
The DNA of this place.

00:14:47.218 --> 00:14:48.658
Ukraine in general...

00:14:49.248 --> 00:14:52.321
I'm gonna say my impressions here
in Kharkiv are like, "Wow."

00:14:52.862 --> 00:14:54.860
A lot of impressive young people.

00:14:54.945 --> 00:14:58.145
DAVID: I think it's the purpose
of your life to do what you like

00:14:58.145 --> 00:15:02.509
because when you can spend
all your life just working on a job

00:15:02.509 --> 00:15:04.300
just making some money

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.976
when you're gonna be like, I don't know,
60 sitting in a chair thinking

00:15:08.976 --> 00:15:11.041
"What for I did spend the whole life?"

00:15:11.041 --> 00:15:12.328
"Just for some money?"

00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:14.609
"And what is that? Stressing?"

00:15:16.567 --> 00:15:17.768
And then there's Victoria.

00:15:17.768 --> 00:15:22.140
She's 17, she went to the US
when she was 15 as an exchange student

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:26.013
and she ends up
in the Deep South of the US.

00:15:26.723 --> 00:15:28.403
And she talks like...

00:15:28.695 --> 00:15:30.254
[Victoria talking in background]

00:15:30.254 --> 00:15:32.699
All her mannerisms,
like everything she does

00:15:32.699 --> 00:15:35.433
She talks like she's from the Deep South.

00:15:35.882 --> 00:15:37.989
I'm sorry, I'm excited.

00:15:39.377 --> 00:15:40.377
My heart...

00:15:40.552 --> 00:15:41.734
All the problems...

00:15:41.734 --> 00:15:44.733
African American family hosted me

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.542
and look what you have.

00:15:47.542 --> 00:15:48.496
[all laughing]

00:15:48.496 --> 00:15:50.885
They've created a monster.

00:15:51.231 --> 00:15:53.034
You know, just talking, blah, blah.

00:15:53.034 --> 00:15:56.326
Myself and then this girl
was thinking she was...

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.063
And then this girl came in...

00:15:58.129 --> 00:16:00.026
She was trying to steal my boyfriend.

00:16:00.026 --> 00:16:03.758
I was like, "What? I'm not even
interested in Mexicans." you know?

00:16:03.758 --> 00:16:05.117
I don't need that.

00:16:05.117 --> 00:16:07.206
My black mother...

00:16:07.206 --> 00:16:10.253
and she said, "Hey, you gotta come
and pick up this girl."

00:16:10.286 --> 00:16:14.544
And everything, we were dancing,
jamming, twerking, you know, a bit...

00:16:14.544 --> 00:16:17.936
And all this stuff,
that was the best experience ever.

00:16:18.124 --> 00:16:19.124
Thank you.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.841
Victoria, yeah I'm future....

00:16:22.018 --> 00:16:23.138
[all laughing]

00:16:23.333 --> 00:16:27.901
But it's cool to have family
in another part of the world.

00:16:28.564 --> 00:16:29.564
[traffic]

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.926
I met this guy here, his name is Bagdan.

00:16:33.926 --> 00:16:37.636
Bagdan has an English language bar.

00:16:37.817 --> 00:16:41.017
Yeah, we can only speak English
and some Ukrainian.

00:16:41.373 --> 00:16:43.528
If you're brain is exploding.

00:16:43.528 --> 00:16:45.528
Like you are tired of English.

00:16:45.795 --> 00:16:48.066
You can turn into Ukrainian, no charge.

00:16:48.066 --> 00:16:50.610
PETER: And so he brings in
all these people from around the world.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.582
It's like super multi-cultural.

00:16:52.582 --> 00:16:54.515
He created a cool world here.

00:16:56.782 --> 00:16:58.852
♪ jazz trumpet ♪

00:17:10.155 --> 00:17:13.126
What makes a place is people,
always does, right?

00:17:13.126 --> 00:17:15.993
And maybe I'm lucky,
maybe I got lucky here.

00:17:16.072 --> 00:17:18.939
I just seem to run into
so many cool people.

00:17:19.917 --> 00:17:23.757
And for those from here,
from this beautiful city, thank you.

00:17:24.228 --> 00:17:27.554
A lot of people reached out
and showed me around.

00:17:27.554 --> 00:17:30.528
-Don't worry about it.
-Only you can understand me.

00:17:31.658 --> 00:17:32.658
[hands slap]

00:17:35.386 --> 00:17:37.066
VICTORIA: What's up, Peter?

00:17:37.172 --> 00:17:38.532
PETER: What's up?

00:17:39.345 --> 00:17:42.079
The sun is up but it's gonna go down soon

00:17:42.708 --> 00:17:44.841
and wanna get a cool time lapse.

00:17:45.858 --> 00:17:50.713
So this bridge situation here in Kharkiv
is quite spectacular.

00:17:52.325 --> 00:17:54.591
♪ busker playing acoustic guitar ♪

00:18:07.855 --> 00:18:08.895
[music fades]

